-http-semantics\",\n          \"instruction\": \"Choose methods and status codes that match operation behavior. Document any retry or idempotency expectations.\",\n          \"verification\": \"Test success, input errors and repeated requests where retries are supported.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"plan-consumer-migrations\",\n          \"instruction\": \"Identify affected consumers and agree on a migration path before making a breaking contract change.\",\n          \"verification\": \"Record the migration decision and run compatibility checks for supported client versions.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fastapi\",\n      \"title\": \"FastAPI services\",\n      \"version\": \"1.0.0\",\n      \"description\": \"Checks for API response schemas, resource lifespan and request behavior.\",\n      \"sources\": [\n        {\n          \"title\": \"FastAPI response models\",\n          \"url\": \"https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/response-model/\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"FastAPI lifespan events\",\n          \"url\": \"https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/events/\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"title\": \"FastAPI testing\",\n          \"url\": \"https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/testing/\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"depends_on\": [\n        \"python\",\n        \"api-design\"\n      ],\n      \"rules\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"declare-response-model\",\n          \"instruction\": \"Declare the response model for JSON endpoints that return application data. Expose the promised fields and keep private persistence fields outside the schema.\",\n          \"verification\": \"Inspect the generated OpenAPI operation and assert the response shape with a representative record containing internal fields.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"manage-resource-lifespan\",\n          \"instruction\": \"Open and close shared resources through the project's FastAPI lifespan mechanism. Keep