nity-solution-trees/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Christensen Institute, Jobs to Be Done Theory\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.christenseninstitute.org/theory/jobs-to-be-done/\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"brain_review\": {\n    \"specialists\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"discovery-lead\",\n        \"title\": \"Product discovery lead\",\n        \"focus\": \"Identify the affected user and their progress in a concrete situation. Compare the observed problem with the proposed solution and the workaround users already use.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"product-analyst\",\n        \"title\": \"Product analyst\",\n        \"focus\": \"Specify the outcome event, eligible population, baseline and decision window. Identify signals that would distinguish adoption from sustained improvement.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"scope-lead\",\n        \"title\": \"Scope and prioritization lead\",\n        \"focus\": \"Define the smallest complete user flow that could test the main assumption. Identify dependencies, deferred cases and the cost of leaving the current flow in place.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"rollout-lead\",\n        \"title\": \"Adoption and rollout lead\",\n        \"focus\": \"Identify groups whose work changes, what support they need and how the team would pause or reverse rollout if friction rises.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      \"Recent support tickets, user interviews or workflow observations showing who encountered the problem, under what conditions and what they tried next.\",\n      \"A current baseline for the target outcome, including eligible users or transactions, time window and known data gaps.\",\n      \"Current workflow, dependencies and acceptance examples for the intended path, including one consequential exception or role boundary.\",\n      \"Existing rollout, support and analytics capabilities that the team can use to test or reverse the change.\"\n    ],\n    \"challenge\": [\n      \"Compare leave as is, improve the existing workflow and deliver a small new slice. Explain which user friction each option addresses.\",\n      \"Test the proposed priority against a counterexample such as a less frequent problem with a greater consequence or a group for whom the workaround already succeeds.\",\n      \"Challenge success numbers that rise when usage grows but leave the target problem unchanged. State the data or experiment needed to separate those effects.\",\n      \"Identify a product assumption that could be tested without building the full feature. Explain which result would change the recommendation.\"\n    ],\n    \"decision_criteria\": [\n      \"Recommend a build when observed demand, a complete first slice and a measurable improvement are supported by the evidence.\",\n      \"Recommend discovery or a pilot when affected users are known but the cause, demand or replacement workflow is still uncertain. Name the test and what would count as enough evidence.\",\n      \"Recommend keeping or improving the current workflow when it addresses the verified need with lower support and maintenance cost.\",\n      \"Condition rollout on a named owner, a baseline and an agreed threshold for pausing or revising the release.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### engineering\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"Engineering\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Review code boundaries, dependencies and compatibility before choosing an implementation.\",\n  \"routing\": [\n    \"Implementation and integration\"\n  ],\n  \"expertises\": [\n    \"Software architecture and integration\",\n    \"Data modeling and migrations\",\n    \"API design and maintainability\"\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [\n    \"Which existing modules and interfaces can handle the change?\",\n    \"What happens to existing data and clients during rollout?\",\n    \"Which contracts or architecture decisions should the change document?\"\n  ],\n  \"source_leads\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"OpenAPI Specification 3.1.2\",\n      \"url\": \"https://spec.openapis.org/oas/v3.1.2.html\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Google Engineering Practices, Code review\",\n      \"url\": \"https://google.github.io/eng-practices/review/reviewer/looking-for.html\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"brain_review\": {\n    \"specialists\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"architecture\",\n        \"title\": \"Software architect\",\n        \"focus\": \"Trace the use case through the existing modules. Choose where the behavior and its dependencies belong and name the owner of any new boundary.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"contracts\",\n        \"title\": \"API and integration engineer\",\n        \"focus\": \"Check changed request, response and event contracts against every supported consumer. Decide which changes need a compatibility path or migration.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"data-consistency\",\n        \"title\": \"Data engineer\",\n        \"focus\": \"Identify the invariants for reads and writes. Check what happens to committed data when work is interrupted, retried or performed concurrently.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"maintainability\",\n        \"title\": \"Code reviewer\",\n        \"focus\": \"Find unnecessary dependencies and duplicated domain logic. Confirm that the proposed change can be verified through the entry points callers use.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      \"Entry point, owning modules, changed behavior and the relevant repository paths or design decision.\",\n      \"Before-and-after public contracts and a list of supported callers or event consumers, with compatibility results for affected versions.\",\n      \"Data schema and migration sequence, with results for existing records, mixed-version rollout and the agreed recovery path where relevant.\",\n      \"Tests or execution traces that show success, a representative partial failure and a retry for operations that can repeat.\",\n      \"Reason for any new service or dependency and the name of the team expected to maintain it.\"\n    ],\n    \"challenge\": [\n      \"Could an existing module own this behavior without introducing a second source of truth?\",\n      \"Which supported caller or previously stored value would behave differently with the proposed change?\",\n      \"What has already been committed if the second step fails, and what happens when the request is retried?\",\n      \"Which edge of the new design requires another team to change or deploy at the same time?\"\n    ],\n    \"decision_criteria\": [\n      \"Prefer the design with a clear owner, the smallest affected boundary and a demonstrated test path for the agreed behavior.\",\n      \"Ask for a migration or consumer approval if a supported API, event or stored shape would break.\",\n      \"Hold the change when a foreseeable failure, retry or concurrent operation can break a data invariant without a verified recovery path.\",\n      \"Record the reason and responsible team when the change adds an operational dependency.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### qa\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"Quality assurance\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Turn acceptance criteria into checks that cover the user flow and likely regressions.\",\n  \"routing\": [\n    \"Acceptance and regression checks\",\n    \"Brief mentions 'tests'\"\n  ],\n  \"expertises\": [\n    \"Risk-based test design\",\n    \"Regression and compatibility testing\",\n    \"Release acceptance and defect triage\"\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [\n    \"Which user paths and boundary conditions need explicit tests?\",\n    \"What fixture or environment would make a failure reproducible?\",\n    \"Which compatibility and regression checks must pass before release?\"\n  ],\n  \"source_leads\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"ISTQB Foundation Level testing syllabus\",\n      \"url\": \"https://istqb.org/certifications/certified-tester-foundation-level-ctfl-v4-0/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"W3C WAI, Evaluating Web Accessibility\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.w3.org/WAI/test-evaluate/\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"brain_review\": {\n    \"specialists\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"test-design\",\n        \"title\": \"Test design lead\",\n        \"focus\": \"Map each important acceptance criterion to an observable result. Prioritize boundary cases and recovery paths that could change the release decision.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n        \"title\": \"Regression engineer\",\n        \"focus\": \"Choose representative legacy data and supported versions. Verify that existing users and integrations can continue through the change.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"exploratory-testing\",\n        \"title\": \"Exploratory tester\",\n        \"focus\": \"Exercise the user journey with realistic interruptions, partial progress and varied input. Include keyboard or assistive technology checks when the changed interface requires them.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"release-acceptance\",\n        \"title\": \"Release QA lead\",\n        \"focus\": \"Assess which results are trustworthy for the candidate revision. Triage defects by user impact and decide which unmet criteria block shipment.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      \"Acceptance criteria mapped to named automated checks or a manual test charter, with expected outcomes.\",\n      \"Build revision, environment, test data description and supported client or browser versions covered by the results.\",\n      \"Coverage of upgraded records and existing flows, with separate results for new records and clean setup where relevant.\",\n      \"Evidence for representative boundary, failure and recovery paths, including a trace or observed outcome for defects.\",\n      \"List of regressions, intermittent failures and untested cases with impact, owner and disposition.\"\n    ],\n    \"challenge\": [\n      \"Which assertion would fail if the interface reported success while the underlying state stayed unchanged?\",\n      \"How would the same test behave for a customer whose records were created before this release?\",\n      \"Which failure only appears after an interruption, a retry or a change in the order of operations?\",\n      \"Could test data, mocks or a successful retry conceal a defect in the supported user environment?\"\n    ],\n    \"decision_criteria\": [\n      \"Recommend release when the agreed high-impact scenarios pass on the candidate and the release owner has reviewed the impact and disposition of the remaining gaps.\",\n      \"Hold release for reproducible data loss, an unavailable critical journey or a broken compatibility promise in scope.\",\n      \"Record a flaky or unrun critical check as missing evidence until the team can explain the result or verify it another way.\",\n      \"Accept a deferral only with documented user impact, a clear workaround or mitigation where applicable, and agreement from the release owner.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### design\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"Product design\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Review the interaction, the chosen design system and the states a user must navigate.\",\n  \"routing\": [\n    \"Customer experience\"\n  ],\n  \"expertises\": [\n    \"Interaction design and usability\",\n    \"Design systems and component states\",\n    \"Accessibility and inclusive design\"\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [\n    \"Which component or pattern in the chosen design system fits this interaction?\",\n    \"How will users recover from empty, invalid or interrupted states?\",\n    \"Can users complete the flow with a keyboard and a supported screen reader?\"\n  ],\n  \"source_leads\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"W3C Web Content Accessibility Guidelines 2.2\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Material Design 3 components\",\n      \"url\": \"https://m3.material.io/components\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Apple Human Interface Guidelines\",\n      \"url\": \"https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"shadcn/ui components\",\n      \"url\": \"https://ui.shadcn.com/docs/components\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"GOV.UK Service Manual, Using moderated usability testing\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gov.uk/service-manual/user-research/using-moderated-usability-testing\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"brain_review\": {\n    \"specialists\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"interaction-designer\",\n        \"title\": \"Interaction designer\",\n        \"focus\": \"Map the task across entry, decision, completion and recovery. Find steps where users could misunderstand scope, status or consequences.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"systems-designer\",\n        \"title\": \"Design systems designer\",\n        \"focus\": \"Locate components and tokens in the project's chosen system. Compare composition and extension against adding a new pattern the team would need to maintain.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"accessibility-specialist\",\n        \"title\": \"Accessibility specialist\",\n        \"focus\": \"Examine how keyboard, zoom and assistive technologies handle the relevant tasks. Identify focus behavior, accessible names and announcements in state changes.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"usability-researcher\",\n        \"title\": \"Usability researcher\",\n        \"focus\": \"Define representative participants and realistic tasks the team can observe. Separate usability observations from issues caused by prototype or test conditions.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      \"Current journey or prototype, target platform, available devices and the content the user sees at each decision.\",\n      \"The project's selected design system and version, existing components and screenshots or examples of their states.\",\n      \"Examples of slow, empty, invalid, interrupted or restricted states that occur in the actual workflow.\",\n      \"Recent user observations and applicable keyboard, focus, text resizing or assistive technology checks for the flow.\"\n    ],\n    \"challenge\": [\n      \"Compare an existing design system pattern with a simpler sequence or platform-native control. State which interaction and maintenance trade-offs justify a new component.\",\n      \"Walk the primary task with a keyboard and one relevant assistive technology configuration. Check where focus and error messages go after a failed submission.\",\n      \"Test what users infer before a destructive or irreversible step and how they resume when the flow is interrupted.\",\n      \"Check whether constrained space, long labels, text resizing or localization changes the reading or action order.\"\n    ],\n    \"decision_criteria\": [\n      \"Use an existing pattern when it communicates the correct task and states, passes relevant accessibility checks and fits the supported platforms.\",\n      \"Propose a new pattern only for a documented interaction gap. Specify its states, validation approach and maintenance owner.\",\n      \"Hold the current recommendation when an observed blocker prevents users from completing or recovering within the flow. Name the evidence that would resolve it.\",\n      \"Prefer a prototype or usability session when different designs make plausible but unverified claims about user understanding.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### marketing\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"Marketing and market research\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Compare competitors and substitutes in the named market before proposing positioning or a launch message.\",\n  \"routing\": [\n    \"Customer expectations and market evidence\"\n  ],\n  \"expertises\": [\n    \"Competitive research and market segmentation\",\n    \"Positioning and launch messaging\",\n    \"Channel selection and measurement\"\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [\n    \"What market, audience and time window should the research cover?\",\n    \"What do dated product pages, release notes, public statements or filings confirm about direct competitors and substitutes?\",\n    \"What can the team substantiate in launch messaging, and which claims need evidence?\"\n  ],\n  \"source_leads\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"U.S. Small Business Administration, Market research and competitive analysis\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sba.gov/counseling/plan-your-business/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"UK Government Communication Service, Campaign lifecycle\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/government-functional-standard-govs-011-communication/government-functional-standard-govs-011-communications#the-campaign-lifecycle\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"brain_review\": {\n    \"specialists\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"market-researcher\",\n        \"title\": \"Market researcher\",\n        \"focus\": \"Define the buyer problem, geography and review period. Compare dated evidence for direct competitors, substitutes and the option of doing nothing.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"positioning-lead\",\n        \"title\": \"Positioning lead\",\n        \"focus\": \"Connect audience needs to a specific value proposition. Identify the proof, scope and qualifications needed for claims about capability, outcomes or differentiation.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"channel-planner\",\n        \"title\": \"Channel planner\",\n        \"focus\": \"Compare how the target audience discovers and evaluates options across channels. Propose a sequence and pilot that fit the budget and production effort.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"measurement-analyst\",\n        \"title\": \"Marketing measurement analyst\",\n        \"focus\": \"Define the observable action and attribution limits. Select a baseline or comparison that can distinguish campaign effects from seasonality and other launches.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      \"Named audience, buying role, market geography, release timing and available campaign capacity.\",\n      \"Approved customer interviews or win-loss notes for the stated problem, with date and segment where available.\",\n      \"Dated product pages, release notes or official statements for relevant competitors. Record the plan, region and version that support each claim.\",\n      \"Approved message claims with their backing release criteria, customer evidence and applicable qualification.\",\n      \"Channel performance baselines, event or reporting definitions and known changes to tracking or visitor mix.\"\n    ],\n    \"challenge\": [\n      \"Test whether the claimed differentiation survives after comparing the same problem, subscription tier, market and time window.\",\n      \"Compare a broader launch, a targeted audience pilot and deferring the launch until an evidence gap closes. State what could change the audience or message.\",\n      \"Challenge claims drawn from a competitor's silence, a small interview sample or traffic without a defined buyer action.\",\n      \"Check if simultaneous launches, seasonality or measurement changes could produce the same outcome without the campaign.\"\n    ],\n    \"decision_criteria\": [\n      \"Recommend a message when the selected audience has a specific evidenced need and every material claim can be supported with appropriately scoped proof.\",\n      \"Recommend a pilot when channel fit, audience behavior or incremental impact is uncertain and one measurable test can resolve it.\",\n      \"Defer a claim when supporting evidence applies to another market, version or audience, or when first-hand evidence remains unavailable.\",\n      \"Recommend a channel only with an owner, a feasible budget and a defined action that the team can measure or validate.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### security\n\n```json\n{\n  \"title\": \"Security and privacy\",\n  \"purpose\": \"Review who can reach the changed systems, which data they can see and which controls need evidence.\",\n  \"routing\": [\n    \"Personal data access\"\n  ],\n  \"expertises\": [\n    \"Application security and access control\",\n    \"Privacy engineering and data handling\",\n    \"Security governance and control evidence\"\n  ],\n  \"questions\": [\n    \"Which actors, permissions and data classes does the change affect?\",\n    \"What controls already cover the new data path, and who owns them?\",\n    \"What verification should a reviewer see before approving the change?\"\n  ],\n  \"source_leads\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"OWASP Application Security Verification Standard\",\n      \"url\": \"https://asvs.owasp.org/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"NIST SP 800-218, Secure Software Development Framework 1.1\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/218/final\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"brain_review\": {\n    \"specialists\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"application-security\",\n        \"title\": \"Application security reviewer\",\n        \"focus\": \"Trace authorization from each affected entry point to the resource it protects. Verify the expected access rules for users, services and background jobs.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"privacy-engineering\",\n        \"title\": \"Privacy engineer\",\n        \"focus\": \"Map personal and sensitive data to its purpose, recipients and retention. Flag fields or transfers that require the data owner's decision.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"release-integrity\",\n        \"title\": \"Software supply chain reviewer\",\n        \"focus\": \"Review changed dependencies, identity scopes and artifact provenance. Determine whether the release evidence applies to the exact build under review.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"control-ownership\",\n        \"title\": \"Security control owner\",\n        \"focus\": \"Match the proposed change to approved controls, available evidence and open exceptions. Identify who can accept a residual risk and when it must be revisited.\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"evidence\": [\n      \"An approved data flow showing the affected actors, systems, trust boundaries, sensitive fields and external recipients.\",\n      \"Access matrix for the changed resources, with results of approved defensive checks for permitted access, denied access and isolation where relevant.\",\n      \"Data owner's decision on purpose, retention, deletion and disclosure, including copies in logs, caches and third-party services.\",\n      \"Changed dependency inventory and relevant advisory, credential or build-provenance review tied to the release revision.\",\n      \"List of applicable controls and open findings, with evidence, owner and approved exception details where available.\"\n    ],\n    \"challenge\": [\n      \"Which affected entry point or background worker can reach the data under a different identity from the main request?\",\n      \"How does the approved role or tenant change take effect for already active sessions and cached access decisions?\",\n      \"Which copies of the data survive the primary deletion flow, and who owns their retention?\",\n      \"Does the evidence cover the exact revision and access scope that will ship?\"\n    ],\n    \"decision_criteria\": [\n      \"Approve the reviewed scope when the asset owner can verify access boundaries and the defensive checks cover the affected roles and resources.\",\n      \"Hold exposure of the changed path when authority, data handling or a required control remains unresolved.\",\n      \"Route exceptions to the named risk owner and record accepted scope, expiration and follow-up evidence.\",\n      \"Describe which controls were reviewed and which evidence remains outstanding when reporting approval.\"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n## Review to record\n\nGive one recommendation per board in the review template. Record unresolved scope, missing evidence and trade-offs. Summarize the proposed next step and any decisions the user needs to make.\n\nFor a brain review, write each specialist finding before forming a verdict. Mark its basis as observed, assumption, or missing, and cite one-based positions from the board's evidence list. Challenge the proposed approach with a realistic alternative and one way it could fail, then name the test or evidence that would change the decision. Preserve disagreement between specialists or boards in the summary.\n\nUse verdict proceed, revise, block, or insufficient-evidence. Use confidence low, medium, or high. A recommendation to proceed or a high confidence rating requires observed findings and cited evidence. For a blocking finding, say who can resolve it and what would clear it.\n",
